 be a little more inclined to  go you know what i was scared to call  this with the old overtime rules but now  i know  patrick mahomes is going to get a chance  i might bring the the corn you know the  free safety weak side linebacker blitz  in this situation and go for it and see  if i can stop the drive right here on a  third and five or whatever it may be i  think it gives the defensive coordinator  a little bit more power uh and not not  necessarily so afraid to blow the game  you know with one aggressive maybe take  a chance type call on the defensive side  yeah look here's where i think the the  decision becomes more challenging in the  regular season because there's only 10  minutes available for overtime if you  choose to kick the ball off and they  drive down the field and score a  touchdown how much time are you going to  have to match it sure if they take six  seven eight minutes you're going to  really be pinched to try to play for a  tie i'd almost rather take the ball  especially if i'm at home well at home  but you know what i'm at home i'm more  likely to kick i think well in the  regular school what you're saying right  there and you just kind of led me into  it you know intentionally again  i think because of what you said you're  worried about that team you know eating  up too much of the clock again since you  know you're gonna get the ball back at  some point i think defenses will take a  chance and go okay they're they're kind  of like bleeding us to death here little  by little let's take a trance and see if  we can get the big sack or try to force  a tuner turnover or whatever it is  either they score okay whatever it be if  they score they score and then at least  we get the ball back with some time to  go down and get a touchdown ourselves uh  but maybe we can make something happen  to where they got a punt or settle for a  long field goal or something like that  if i'm at home in a loud stadium in the  regular season i'm going to be more 